diff --git a/collab/scenarios/71-undo-gives-a-fetched-window-its-place-back.sim b/collab/scenarios/71-undo-gives-a-fetched-window-its-place-back.sim
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cb8aaa06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/collab/scenarios/71-undo-gives-a-fetched-window-its-place-back.sim
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Story: somebody keeps Mail parked at the right edge of the screen, a third of it showing, out of the way. They look something up in
+# it: Arbor's menu, Windows, Mail. It comes in whole, as asked. Done with it, they want it where it was, and press the key that takes
+# things back everywhere else. (BOARD 1.91. Window ids start at 101; the display is 1440 by 900.)
+quiet
+open Safari
+open Notes
+open Mail 400x300
+move 103 1300 500 400 300
+focus 101
+# Nothing has been done yet that could be taken back.
+undo
+expect fail
+# Of Mail 140 points show, and the list says so. A click, and it is in by the shortest way, at its own size.
+menu
+expect replied Mail: Mail 103  [out of view]
+menu-choose Mail
+expect ok
+expect at 103 1040 500 400x300
+expect focused 103
+# The menu names the step in a word a person knows.
+menu
+expect replied Undo Move
+# One step, one move, and it is at its edge again.
+undo
+expect ok
+expect moved-once
+expect at 103 1300 500 400x300
+# And it stays there, whatever is laid out next.
+dock 101 left
+zoom 101
+show-all
+expect at 103 1300 500 400x300
+# Those were steps of their own. Taken back, Mail is still where its person wants it.
+undo
+expect ok
+expect floating 101
+expect at 103 1300 500 400x300
+# Redo brings nothing of Mail's: the dock replaced what could be put back.
+# Asked for again, in Go to… this time, it comes in again, and goes back again.
+find Mail
+expect ok
+expect at 103 1040 500 400x300
+undo
+expect ok
+expect at 103 1300 500 400x300
+redo
+expect ok
+expect at 103 1040 500 400x300
+# Moved by hand since, it stays where the hand put it: Undo takes back what Arbor did, not what its person has done.
+move 103 200 400 400 300
+undo
+expect fail
+expect at 103 200 400 400x300
+# Going to a window that is whole is no change to anything.
+menu-choose Notes
+expect ok
+menu
+expect replied Undo ⌃⌥Z (gray)
+# Parked so far out that no hand could get hold of it (10 points show), it is fetched for good: Arbor puts no window there. Whoever
+# has just seen Mail move and presses the key means Mail: it says so once, moves nothing, and names what the next press takes back.
+# The menu's row names nothing that it will not do: it says what is older, as after a window has closed.
+dock 101 left
+move 103 1430 500 400 300
+focus 101
+menu-choose Mail
+expect ok
+expect at 103 1040 500 400x300
+menu
+expect replied Undo Dock
+press undo
+expect fail
+expect said That move cannot be undone · ⌃⌥Z again undoes Dock
+expect docked 101
+expect at 103 1040 500 400x300
+press undo
+expect ok
+expect floating 101
